artifacts/
*.asv
*.mat.cache
__pycache__/

# Real PO.DAAC products are supplied through the READING_DATA_POOL
# variable, not committed: the five large ones are ~60 MB together and
# actions/checkout removes untracked files with git clean -ffdx anyway,
# so a copy dropped into the working tree would not survive a run. The
# two small bundled products are excepted explicitly; they are already
# tracked, this only guards against an accidental re-add.
tests/realdata/*.txt
tests/realdata/*.txt.gz
!tests/realdata/MAS1B_2020-01-01_C_04.txt
!tests/realdata/THR1B_2020-01-01_C_04.txt

# The five ITSG fixtures are the first 60 records of the real TU Graz
# products with the record-count line adjusted to match; headers and record
# text are byte-for-byte as published. ~58 KB together, so they are bundled
# and the format is covered without the data pool. The full days go in
# READING_DATA_POOL like the large PO.DAAC products.
!tests/realdata/GRACEFO-1_*.txt

# The two official event lists (G-05) are extracts of the published
# TN-01 / TN-01a files, ~8 KB together. They must be excepted by name:
# the "*.txt" rule above would otherwise drop them silently, and the
# only symptom would be testEventLists failing in CI on a fixture that
# is present in every working tree.
!tests/realdata/TN-01_SOE.txt
!tests/realdata/TN-01a_SCE.txt

# The hybrid transplant accelerometer fixture (G-04, issue #19) is the
# first 120 records of the published GRACE D file, ~25 KB. Same trap as
# the two above: the "*.txt" rule would drop it silently and the only
# symptom would be testACH1B failing in CI on a file that is present in
# every working tree.
!tests/realdata/ACH1B_2020-01-01_D_04.txt

# The classic GRACE fixtures are binary (".dat"), so no rule above
# touches them; they are named here so the set is visible in one place.
# Seven RL02 products of 2008-01-01 plus the two RL03 files, first 40
# records each, NUMBER OF DATA RECORDS rewritten to match, ~54 KB
# together. See tests/realdata/README.md.
!tests/realdata/*.dat
